{
  "goal": "Get students to download Gauth and try one feature on their own homework or notes: step-by-step explanations, or notes turned into flashcards and a quiz.",
  "angle": "Start in a real study moment: late at night, stuck, behind, stressed. Then show Gauth explaining the problem step by step or turning your notes into a quiz. The payoff is relief and understanding, never a grade, a GPA or a shortcut.",
  "hooks": [
    "It's 11pm and I still have to finish this problem set, so I opened Gauth.",
    "I'm cooked. This is the only reason I understand this chapter.",
    "Toxic study motivation: Lock in. No one is coming to save you. Open Gauth.",
    "Gauth, wait, explain that again. Break it down like I'm 12.",
    "When I'm having the best time planning my lock in… then remember I actually have to do the work."
  ],
  "mustInclude": [
    "Mark the post as a paid partnership or add #ad.",
    "Tag #gauthpartner.",
    "Say or show the name Gauth in the first five seconds. If you use a hands-busy or end-reveal format, put the name on screen as text or keep the app visible in the shot early.",
    "Open mid-scene: at your desk, late at night, stuck, behind. Stress first, then relief.",
    "Show the app working on screen: a step-by-step explanation, notes turned into flashcards, a practice quiz, or an AI Course lesson.",
    "Real student style. Useful beats polished."
  ],
  "avoid": [
    "Any promise of better grades. No \"4.0 GPA\", \"ace your exams\", \"you'll pass\", \"grade rescue\" or \"how do you keep your grades so high\".",
    "Anything that makes Gauth look like a way to cheat. No using it during an exam, no \"finish homework faster\" or \"just copy the answer\".",
    "Skits mocking teachers or showing students sneaking help in class.",
    "\"What's your GPA?\" street interviews that tie a high GPA to the app.",
    "Any claims about privacy, data or the app being \"safe\". Don't reply to comments on this topic. Flag them to us."
  ],
